---
source: tests/snapshots.rs
description: grav export --help
expression: run(args)
---
exit: 0
--- stdout
Write a complete scan as a JSON snapshot

Usage: grav export [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]
          Directory to scan, or a snapshot saved by `grav export` or `ncdu -o`
          
          [default: .]

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Scanning:
  -A, --apparent-size
          Count file lengths instead of disk usage

  -l, --count-links
          Count every hard link to a file, not only the first

  -L, --follow-symlinks
          Follow symbolic links

      --cross-fs
          Descend into other filesystems [default: stay on the scanned one]

      --no-hidden
          Skip entries whose names start with "."

  -e, --exclude <GLOB>
          Skip entries matching GLOB, by name or by path from the root (repeatable)

  -j, --threads <N>
          Scanning threads [default: one per CPU]

      --git
          Annotate entries with Git status

      --max-entries <N>
          Fail if the scan reaches more than N entries

Output:
  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Snapshot format

          Possible values:
          - json: The complete tree in versioned JSON, readable by every grav command
          - ncdu: An ncdu dump, readable by `ncdu -f` and `gdu -f`
          
          [default: json]

  -o, --output <FILE>
          Write to FILE instead of standard output, replacing it atomically; compressed with zstd if
          FILE ends in .zst

      --strict
          Exit with status 3 if anything could not be read

Global options:
      --color <WHEN>
          When to use colour
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --binary
          Show sizes in powers of 1024 (KiB, MiB) instead of 1000 (kB, MB)

      --log-file <FILE>
          Append diagnostic logs to FILE (filter with RUST_LOG)
          
          [env: GRAVITYFILE_LOG_FILE]
--- stderr
